WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:04.567
To cut a useful section of a zebrafish

00:00:04.567 --> 00:00:08.585
specimen, orientation and compatible embedding materials must work together.

00:00:14.175 --> 00:00:19.348
The specimen was oriented in an agarose pre-embedding support before

00:00:19.348 --> 00:00:24.522
subsequent paraffin processing. The hoped-for geometry depended on their compatibility.

00:00:31.425 --> 00:00:34.403
Agarose and paraffin did not form

00:00:34.403 --> 00:00:37.380
the coherent embedding system the microtome needed.

00:00:41.800 --> 00:00:45.390
Material separation frustrated sectioning. There was

00:00:45.390 --> 00:00:48.980
no interpretable histological slice from that attempt.

00:00:54.008 --> 00:00:58.686
The images identify an upstream materials bottleneck. A

00:00:58.686 --> 00:01:03.364
changed processing protocol needs its own experimental verification.

00:01:09.675 --> 00:01:14.104
This is not a success story about histopathology. It is

00:01:14.104 --> 00:01:18.534
the story of what an incompatible preparation taught us to investigate.
